{{#is_alert}}
## What's happening?
The OPW disk buffer volume on `{{host.name}}` in pipeline `{{pipeline_name.name}}` has only **{{value}}** of its capacity free. A buffer volume that reaches 100% causes partial writes that corrupt the buffer, after which the worker enters CrashLoopBackOff and recovery requires deleting the PVC. Act before it fills.
{{/is_alert}}{{#is_warning}}
## What's happening?
The OPW disk buffer volume on `{{host.name}}` in pipeline `{{pipeline_name.name}}` has only **{{value}}** of its capacity free, below the 30% warning threshold. A volume that fills completely corrupts the buffer and forces a PVC delete to recover.
{{/is_warning}}
{{#is_recovery}}Free space on the OPW disk buffer volume recovered on `{{host.name}}` in pipeline `{{pipeline_name.name}}`.{{/is_recovery}}

